Take a wild guess as to what it is about:
1) [b]New arm![/b] It allows you to record footage of your ecosystem and fast-replay it, hours turned into minutes. Why has your creature gone extinct? How has this chromosome become bigger than the transformer? Why is tigerfish the only one left alive?
- now you can see exactly, why;

2) [b]Tutorial tweaks:[/b] You now have to actually prove your chromosome is viable before sending it off;
The tutorial now waits for the helper to get in hearing range before progressing;
The helper is shown as an indicator icon when off-screen (turns on after it gets the ability to move);
There are now visual warnings for properly setting up the incubator and the transformer;

3) [b]Bugfixes.[/b] Listing it would make this announcement too long, but the main one is the molecules aren't supposed to collapse into a singularity, anymore. Let us know if we made any new bugs! 

Just a little something to tie you over for the holidays xoxo
